    <abstract id="aspace_0d6347cc7e74cf18c3522c9e4a32f1ba" label="Abstract">Harvey Sacks (d.1975) taught in the Department of Sociology at UC Irvine, UC Berkeley and UC Los Angeles (ca. 1960s-72). He is best known for his work in ethnomethodology and conversational analysis. The collection consists of notes, drafts, diaries, unpublished lectures, tapes, lectures, and miscellaneous materials related to Sacks' life and work.</abstract>
    <physloc id="aspace_cdb9778a507267cf851b4a47120258ac">Stored off-site. All requests to access special collections material must be made in advance using the request button located on this page.</physloc>
